## Structural Map

Key files Claude reads first:
- `config/routes.rb` — the HTTP surface
- `app/controllers/` — thin controllers; strong parameters
- `app/services/` — business logic (service objects)
- `app/models/` — Active Record models, validations, scopes
- `db/migrate/` — migrations (reviewed before merge)
- `spec/` or `test/` — RSpec or Minitest

Layers and their purpose:
- `controllers/` → Parameters, authorisation, call a service, render
- `services/` → Business logic and side effects (payments, emails, jobs)
- `models/` → Persistence, validations, associations
- `spec/` → Real-persistence-path request specs for P1/P2 (see `ruby-patterns.md`)

